OL,3,GNEWSABiologist taking on climate change
OL,4,Awith new maize
OL,5,
OL,6,FA biologist has been handed #2.8m to
OL,7,Fdevelop high-yielding maize that uses
OL,8,Fless water, to help farmers fight
OL,9,Fclimate change.
OL,11,FThe four-year project will see
OL,12,FUniversity of Essex academic Dr John
OL,13,FFerguson create new varieties of the
OL,14,Fcrop, which is a vital source of food
OL,15,Facross the world.
OL,17,FHe hopes these new hybrids will then be
OL,18,Fdeveloped to support industrial
OL,19,Fagriculture and subsistence farming
OL,20,Fwithin Sub-Saharan Africa.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
